WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.960
Going into Avengers: Endgame, fans were prepared
for everything; the surviving squad pulling

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.810
off an epic mission, fallen heroes getting
un-dusted and returning to the world of the

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.019
living, Thanos tasting his just desserts,
and much more.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:16.029
They were also bracing themselves for the
possibility that some who were spared in Thanos'

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:20.270
universe-decimating Snap in Avengers: Infinity
War would sadly not make it to the end this

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.270
time around.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.340
If you haven't figured it out by now, there
are major Avengers: Endgame spoilers incoming.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.040
Still here?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.980
Let's continue.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.120
Endgame featured fewer deaths than anyone
had anticipated.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.340
Of the deaths in the movie, one was heroic
and heart-wrenching, another wasn't so much

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.240
a passing away as it was a passing on, and
one was completely unexpected.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.360
It's that last one that we need to talk about.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.640
It's time to address what happened to Black
Widow in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.920
In the first act of the film, Black Widow
serves as a strong leader who keeps the surviving

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:51.710
Avengers in contact with one another five
years after the Decimation.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.819
She organizes meetings at Avengers HQ, checking
in with the other heroes around the galaxy

00:00:55.819 --> 00:00:59.389
to receive status updates on how the Earth
and other worlds are faring.

00:00:59.389 --> 00:01:03.589
Black Widow also makes it her personal mission
to track down her fellow original Avenger

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:09.210
Clint Barton, who abandoned his Hawkeye identity
and assumed his ruthless Ronin persona after

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.040
the snap took his wife and children.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.880
All this felt like Endgame was showing viewers
that Black Widow could rise to the occasion

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.530
to marshal the Avengers and company after
they complete their Time Heist.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.730
If one or all of her teammates bit the dust,
Black Widow could step up to continue leading

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:23.750
the Avengers.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.860
She has the skill and the personality, and
she's been acting as a de-facto supervisor

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.520
of the team for five whole years.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.200
That's not how things pan out.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.000
Black Widow never gets the chance to continue
leading the way.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.250
She doesn't even get to finish the heroes'
mission to travel back to the present day,

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.670
because Black Widow is the first hero to die
in Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.570
Her death comes when she and Hawkeye head
back a few years into the past and touch down

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.740
on Vormir, the remote planet where the Soul
Stone is located.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:52.480
As everyone knows, in order to acquire the
Soul Stone, one must make an equal exchange:

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.280
"A soul for a soul."

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.380
Thanos tossed his adoptive daughter Gamora
off the cliff on Vormir to call the Soul Stone

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.240
his own, and Black Widow and Hawkeye must
do something similar in Endgame.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.860
It's either her or him, they can't both survive
and get the Soul Stone.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.379
Black Widow makes the bold decision to sacrifice
herself and allow Hawkeye to retrieve the

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:19.730
Soul Stone, help the Avengers bring the dusted
back to life, and reunite with his family.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.189
And we know she dies: the film shows Black
Widow laying motionless on the ground, blood

00:02:24.189 --> 00:02:25.500
pooling around her head.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.820
Longtime MCU fans are understandably pretty
upset and confused about it.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.219
While the movie made it seem like there's
little chance Black Widow can be revived,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.640
this isn't actually the end for the hero in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.279
Marvel Studios is working on a Black Widow
solo movie, directed by Australian filmmaker

00:02:41.279 --> 00:02:46.069
Cate Shortland, and is likely aiming to release
it in theaters sometime in the next few years.

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:50.409
Details about the film's plot are sparse right
now, but it's reportedly planned to be a prequel

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:55.319
set just after 2010's Iron Man 2 and before
the events of 2012's Avengers.

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:59.249
Meanwhile, other reports claim that Black
Widow partially takes place in the time when

00:02:59.249 --> 00:03:04.209
Natasha served as an agent for the Soviet
Union's KGB organization, and then skips ahead

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:08.080
to 15 years after the fall of the KGB in the
1980s.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.260
Marvel has yet to confirm any story specifics,
though a prequel-slash-origin-story set-up

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:14.560
sounds pretty plausible.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.599
That would allow for an easy explanation as
to why Black Widow is back on the big screen.

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:22.481
The studio could also use the same digital
de-aging technology it did with Samuel L.

00:03:22.481 --> 00:03:27.980
Jackson for his role as Nick Fury in Captain
Marvel, which is set in 1995, to make Johansson

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.379
look younger for a Black Widow origin story.

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:34.849
Meanwhile, Avengers: Endgame isn't the true
end of Phase 3 of the MCU, there's still time

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:37.300
for the franchise to hint at what's next for
Black Widow.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.219
She has connections to S.H.I.E.L.D. and to
Nick Fury, having joined the team after working

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:46.290
for the KGB, and we know Fury and Agent Maria
Hill will appear in the real Phase 3-closer:

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.720
Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:52.260
It's possible the upcoming film could weave
in mentions of Black Widow's past, or feature

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.780
a post-credits scene set a few decades in
the past that teases the Black Widow solo

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.860
movie.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.699
After all, a Black Widow is a kind of spider.

00:03:59.699 --> 00:04:00.769
Then again… maybe not.

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:04.629
It's all a mystery for now, but fans should
find comfort in knowing that they haven't

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:08.720
seen the last of Black Widow, even after her
devastating death in Endgame.

